# Toits01 "Follow Major Jones" player-input route (item50, extended by item53).
# Player input only (goto/forward/track/fire/wait_travel); no set_goal, no take_control.
# The labelled teleports cover measured impassables: the ladder-top landing traps the walk
# inside LadderVolume0, the start roof has no walkable exit to the courtyard, the deck's east
# parapet blocks walk and jump, the ramp lip and the window gap, the roof dip strip with a
# 50-UU hole, the east roof's trapped edge over a 486 pit, and the warehouse doorway blocked
# by the Movable2 crate (probe12-probe20 logs under local/re/item50/).
#
# Measured outcome: the route reaches TouchTrigger10 (r700 at 18812,1118,791) and the game's
# own Touch fires, but goal 0 does not complete: XIII's TouchTrigger.Touch requires
# self.bActif, and TT10 is authored bActif=false (bActivableParTrigger=true, Tag
# PorteDebloquee) - it arms only when BreakableMover12 (the generator, Health 50, inside the
# walled yard) is destroyed. The yard is sealed by the ForeverLocked door line and the
# through-window shot does not land in the current sim (see the item50 report).
# item53: the route now enters the TT17 zone (r90 at -5010,1337,1009) after the scene's
# 56.7 DonneGrappinStart gate. The grapple demonstration completes (the VM's scripted-physics
# integration runs the demo's Walking/Projectile/Flying moves; measured probe23 under
# local/re/item53/): the demonstrator reaches STA_Retract, fires JonesHookEnd at ~71.5 and
# the handover returns the controller to PlayerWalking (the item50 permanent freeze is gone).
# The Cine0 scene advances past the demo wait to action[117] (movseqb toward PositionInfo118),
# where it stays: the NPC's own traverse across the grapple descent is blocked in the sim (a
# separate measured blocker, distinct from the fixed demo wedge).
# - ladder-top replaced by a labelled teleport onto the roof: the landing traps the
#   walk inside LadderVolume0 (the slide-in distance is nondeterministic; jumps get
#   swallowed in climb state; measured probe13/14/15)
# - courtyard uses the AI west corridor (x~-1450): the (-1400,1350) approach runs
#   into the (-1227,1182) stall (measured probe15)
# - roof->terrace descent replaced by a teleport: the 1167 roof's east edge drops
#   onto a trapped ledge and a pit at 486 (measured probe15, -43 hp)
t=0.50 goto -6300 1383
t=6.00 goto -5720 1385
t=11.00 goto -5608 1387
# labelled teleport (the ladder-top landing traps walking inside LadderVolume0)
t=17.00 teleport -5440 1400 1010
t=17.10 forward 0
t=19.00 goto -5300 1400
t=24.00 goto -4900 1450
t=28.00 forward 0
# item53: the scene arms TT17 (Tag DonneGrappinStart) at its ~56.7 gate; enter the zone after
# the gate and stand through the grapple demonstration (the player is NoControl while the
# demo runs; the handover releases the controller at ~71.5, measured probe23)
t=56.80 goto -5010 1337
t=58.00 forward 0
# released by STA_Retract; the scene's [117] walk ends at PositionInfo0 (-3335,1241) and its
# [118] 'event SpeechJones11' arms TouchTrigger24 (r220 at -3609,1316,2263, z band 2163-2363,
# on the grapple-landing roof ~1200 above the player's start roof). Enter its zone after the
# arm (measured probe72/74, local/re/item62/): the arrival Touch fires 'SpeechJones11Ttempo'
# -> CineTrigger20 (BufferTrigger) -> 'SpeechJones11T' releases the demo's
# 'wait event SpeechJones11T' (a teleport before ~85 is refused by the controller's
# NoControl window, measured probe73).
t=74.00 goto -4940 1420
# item64 grapple #1: the player's own hook replaces the grapple-landing teleport. item64f: the
# game gives the player the Hook itself (the grapple demo scene's XIIIItems.GiveTo of Hook1 at
# ~58.8 with the live level clock; measured local/re/item64f/probe3.txt), so the old
# route-side grant is gone: the retail item-cycle press (DefUser.ini InventoryNext ->
# cNextItem -> bWaitForWeaponMode -> SwitchWeaponMode) puts the fists down and brings the
# Hook up in item mode. Aim at HookPoint0 (-4883,1508,2734; RopeLength 1900,
# ~1756 UU from the roof), fire: the exec Fire -> UseMe spawns HookProjectile +
# HookLink, GoHooking sets bHooked, the +0.25s Timer starts the climb (HookUpSpeed 150/s) and
# the PlayerWalking.ProcessMove taut-rope constraint reels the pawn in (VM-owned while it
# hangs). ~11 s from ~1800 to the 150 minimum. No ClimbableHookNavPoint is authored on
# Toits01 (measured, local/re/item64/toits01-props.txt), so the rope-top handoff never fires;
# the only player-initiated detach is the use key (Grab's bHooked branch -> Hook.Release).
t=85.00 next_item
t=85.80 track HookPoint0
# attach (the fire edge: exec -> ActivatedByFire -> ActivateItem -> Idle.Activate -> UseMe;
# HookLength locks at max(VSize(HookPoint-Pawn),50) = ~1806 < RopeLength 1900). While Walking
# the first HookInUse.Tick consumes the UseMe bGoDown payout request (stops it and clears the
# ActivatedBy* flags), so a continuous hold never climbs: the retail input is a fresh fire
# press, whose ActivateItem re-arms the 0.25 s Timer -> bGoUp + Enable('Tick').
t=86.50 fire_hold 1
t=86.70 fire_hold 0
# climb: HookInUse.Tick ReduceRopeLength (150 UU/s) shortens the rope; each PlayerWalking.
# ProcessMove (0x0237) then pulls the pawn up the excess (SetPhysics Falling + Pawn.Move +
# the radial velocity projection) - (1806-150)/150 = ~11 s to the 150 rope floor.
t=87.00 fire_hold 1
t=98.50 fire_hold 0
# swing east across the roof gap: the anchor (-4883,1508,2733) hangs west of the Model71 roof
# (z=2160, x=-4512..-3490), so the descent must carry horizontal speed. The payout (300 UU/s,
# 1.55 s -> rope ~615) plus the ProcessMove air accel (aForward 32768 -> Acceleration 327 after
# the 0.01 scale) drives the pendulum; the arc crosses the edge ~10.5 s in rising through
# z~2400. Detach on the upswing (the use key: Grab's bHooked branch -> Hook.Release; deselection
# does NOT release the rope - measured, the HookInUse.Tick keeps running after cNextItem) and
# drop onto the roof ~(-3910,858).
t=99.00 yaw -9
t=99.30 altfire_hold 1
t=99.30 forward 1
t=100.85 altfire_hold 0
t=113.00 use
# walk the landing roof into the TT24 zone (r220 at -3609,1316,2263; armed by the scene's
# SpeechJones11 chain at ~81.2 - the arrival Touch fires it, same as the pre-item64 teleport run)
t=112.00 goto -3609 1316
t=119.00 forward 0
# item64f: HookPoint2 is gated by the level's own progression. MapInfo.Timer ->
# Toits01.FirstFrame sets HookPointToActive(HookPoint2).bInteractive = false (with the live
# level clock the Timer now fires; the frozen clock never ran it, which is why the item64
# run attached without the gate), and only Toits01.SetGoalComplete(99) re-enables it. Goal
# 99 is XIIIGoalTrigger6 (Tag 'transmutation'), triggered ONLY by the 'GrappinPoint' crank
# XIIIMoverVarTime1 (TriggerControl; FinishedOpening -> TriggerEvent('transmutation')),
# and 'GrappinPoint' is ONLY Jones's scene action [189] (after his kick, [187]) - which
# waits for [149] 'wait player 75' (the player at Jones's side; [156]/[158] 'give 4/5'
# hand over the sniper rifle) and [179] 'wait event counter_finact1' (CineTrigger1
# CounterTrigger, InitialCounterValue 2: both 'Activation_Sc1_Snipers' GenNMI snipers'
# Bases_Event 'finact1'). Measured (local/re/item64f/probe6.txt): crank Trigger 144.367,
# XIIIGoalTrigger6.Trigger + SetGoalComplete(99) 145.183, HookPoint2.bInteractive true.
# The landing at ~114.3 enters TT24's armed zone; the scene holds the player (FPC) until
# its RPC at 120.2 (SwitchWeapon(0): the Hook is put down).
t=119.10 forward 0
# Jones's spot after his [143] walk ends (~124.9; (-4120,2218)): stand inside 75 UU.
t=120.30 goto -4090 2175
t=126.00 forward 0
# [150] FPC -> [156]/[158] give FusilSnipe + bmg50 ammo -> [161] RPC (~129.1). Select the
# rifle (InventoryGroup 14) and take the stand where the first sniper's fire reached the
